00:00:07:980 - 00:00:14:120
The Supra is Toyota's ultimate expression of performance: For years I've been redefining the

00:00:14:120 - 00:00:19:520
sports car concept because each Supra shares the same basic fundamentals a

00:00:19:520 - 00:00:25:200
Smooth inline six-cylinder engine, rear-wheel drive and a modern chassis, let's review its past

00:00:25:200 - 00:00:31:120
to see how the brand evolved from a grand touring vehicle to the ideal car for a demanding driver.

00:00:32:360 - 00:00:36:840
The history of the Supra begins in 1978 with the Celica,

00:00:36:960 - 00:00:41:700
which provided the basis for the original first generation of the Toyota Supra, the A40.

00:00:41:960 - 00:00:49:060
To create a true grand touring beast, Toyota's plan was to turn it into a competitor to the very popular Dantzum,

00:00:49:160 - 00:00:50:000
now as Nissan.

00:00:50:240 - 00:00:54:580
Toyota engineers used the Celica Leafback as a starting point,

00:00:54:580 - 00:01:02:080
But they made the chassis longer, added an advanced inline 6-cylinder engine, and incorporated the latest in technology and comfort.

00:01:03:660 - 00:01:09:420
The second generation of the Supra, the A60, was a version that Toyota redesigned and improved.

00:01:09:480 - 00:01:16:260
In Japan this model was known as the Celica XX, but the name Celica Supra was used for the world market.

00:01:16:500 - 00:01:21:560
This version was offered in two options, LTP and the performance-focused PTP.

00:01:21:560 - 00:01:28:800
Its splendid 80s design was even more accentuated thanks to its crisp lines and retractable headlights.

00:01:28:920 - 00:01:39:920
The P model would lay the foundation for the Supra's dedication to pure performance, with larger wheels and tires, outstanding fiberglass lights, and optional aerodynamic features.

00:01:39:920 - 00:01:46:080
Another difference was the inline 6-cylinder engine, as well as an increase in length and wheelbase.

00:01:47:600 - 00:01:57:980
With the introduction of its third generation in 1986, the Supra became a standalone model, as the ties between the Celica and the Supra were severed

00:01:57:980 - 00:02:05:120
That allowed Toyota's engineers to design a car from scratch, with pure performance as one of the main goals

00:02:05:120 - 00:02:11:800
The engine was upgraded to a more powerful 3-liter inline engine, rated at 200 horsepower

00:02:11:800 - 00:02:26:980
In doing so, the A70 was not only a four-wheel showcase of the latest technology, but it was also the first Supra to include a turbocharged engine, variable air induction for improved power, and electronically adjustable dampers.

00:02:30:480 - 00:02:41:040
A sports car, an icon and a cultural phenomenon. That's the fourth generation of the A80. This redesign made Toyota put great emphasis on a more serious, high-performance car.

00:02:41:040 - 00:02:48:220
A machine that represents boldness and modernity, today as much as it did when it first came on the market in 1993.

00:02:48:820 - 00:02:55:660
In addition to offering an exquisite blend of style, technology and performance, it boasts a near-perfect weight balance.

00:02:55:680 - 00:03:02:140
An impressive 2JZ naturally aspirated engine with a power of 220 horsepower.

00:03:02:240 - 00:03:08:960
And a Twin Turbo version with a power output of 276 horsepower and an inimitable sound.

00:03:08:960 - 00:03:14:720
For these and several reasons, the A80 is a legend of the road that will always remain current.

00:03:17:160 - 00:03:26:060
The fifth generation, codenamed A90, is based on the well-received FT1 concept, which first appeared in 2014.

00:03:26:600 - 00:03:32:020
It's a rare example of concept car styling that reaches production virtually watered down.

00:03:32:020 - 00:03:40:620
Toyota claims that the design elements also reference the fourth-generation Supra and the 1967 2000GT sports car.

00:03:41:500 - 00:03:46:440
It may be a reservoir for Toyota's performance heritage, but under appearances,

00:03:46:600 - 00:03:55:900
shares a platform with the BMW Z4, has the same powertrain as a BMW M40i and a turbocharged inline 6-cylinder engine,

00:03:55:900 - 00:03:59:500
Rated at 335 horsepower

00:03:59:500 - 00:04:03:760
That's more than enough to go from 0 to 100 in 4.1 seconds

00:04:03:760 - 00:04:04:600
According to Toyota

00:04:04:600 - 00:04:08:080
It also has traction that drives the rear wheels

00:04:08:080 - 00:04:11:120
Through an 8-speed automatic transmission

00:04:11:120 - 00:04:13:740
Toyota did not mention availability of a manual one

00:04:13:740 - 00:04:18:560
Without a doubt, this is something that many of the audience has been unhappy with

00:04:18:560 - 00:04:21:880
Since it loses the essence of what the legendary Supra is

00:04:21:880 - 00:04:23:820
Let's wait if a manual version comes out

00:04:23:820 - 00:04:27:080
for all those males who want to run at full speed.